@flexiarg creativity-commons/low-cost-local-conflict-arenas
@title Low-Cost Local Conflict Arenas
@keywords conflict resolution, edit wars, escalation, modularity, integration cost, Ostrom 6
@audience institution designers, maintainers, agent operators
@tone normative
@style pattern
@grade principle
@provenance Ostrom design principle 6 (conflict-resolution mechanisms), as transposed in Corneli 2016 (ICCC 2016), Table 2 and section "6. Conflict-resolution mechanisms" (Wikipedia edit wars; Heylighen 2015; Benkler 2002; Jakobson 1960). Drafted by claude-16 with Joe, 2026-10-29. Derived from the paper, not mined from runs.
@transposes institutions/conflict-resolution-mechanisms
@status draft 2026-10-29; runs correct it
@references [creativity-commons/ARGUMENT creativity-commons/formative-sanctions creativity-commons/nested-places]

! conclusion:
  Producers have rapid access to low-cost local arenas to resolve
  conflicts, with a higher authority for the cases those arenas cannot
  settle.

  + context:
    Wikipedia's edit wars are fought on article pages and settled on
    talk pages, using machine-generated metadata throughout; the
    unresolvable cases go to site-wide policy or arbitration. Peer
    production needs modules that are fine-grained and cheap to
    integrate.

  + IF:
    Producers' work can collide, by editing the same thing or by
    pursuing incompatible goals.

  + HOWEVER:
    A local arena that is too cheap settles nothing; escalating too
    readily loads the higher authority with cases it need not see.

  + THEN:
    Make conflict detectable by the Producers themselves (two changes to
    one region; two goals that cannot both hold). Give each conflict a
    local place to be discussed next to the work, record what settled
    it, and name the higher authority for what stays unsettled. Plan the
    work in small modules so conflicts are rare and cheap to integrate.

  + BECAUSE:
    Conflicts settled where they arise cost little and teach the people
    involved; a named escalation path stops them festering.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    next[Example: 8 fork branches touch sh-script.el; detect that before merging, not during.]
    next[Example: when bells between agents cross, switch to a whistle; the blocking call is the local arena.]
    next[Example: a debbugs thread is the local arena; emacs-devel and the maintainers are the higher authority.]
